# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# §6: unit_make_adder_size_t.lm2 under --walk-methods. A capture keeps its type: n is a size_t
# formal, the node's field n is a size_t cell (l2_mcap_value_helper/l2_own_store_helper dispatch
# by l2_mcap_ty, not always int). addBig(2^32)=101, addSmall(2^32-1)=2. Mutant: an int cell
# instead -- 2^32 truncates to 0, addBig: 1 becomes 2, not 101 -- exit 0.
fn: makeAdder (size_t: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        if: n > 4294967295U
            return: x + 100
        return: x + 1
    return: addN

@: addBig makeAdder(4294967296U)
@: addSmall makeAdder(4294967295U)
int: a (addBig: 1)
int: b (addSmall: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 101 && b = 2
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
